    "['ip dhcp pool [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set system services dhcp pool BAS-POOL network 192.168.0.0/24', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set system services dhcp pool BAS-POOL network 192.168.0.0/24', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent Juniper configuration for the DHCP pool:\\n##\\nset system services dhcp pool BAS-POOL network 192.168.0.0/24\\nset system services dhcp pool BAS-POOL default-router 192.168.0.1\\nset system services dhcp pool BAS-POOL name-server 8.8.8.8\\nset system services dhcp pool BAS-POOL name-server 8.8.4.4\\nset system services dhcp pool BAS-POOL lease-time infinite\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, there isn\\'t a direct single command equivalent to Cisco\\'s \"ip dhcp pool\" that includes all parameters. The configuration is broken down into individual statements for each parameter under the DHCP pool.', 'trans_template': 'set system services dhcp pool BAS-POOL network 192.168.0.0/24'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set system services dhcp pool BAS-POOL default-router 192.168.0.1', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set system services dhcp pool BAS-POOL default-router 192.168.0.1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent Juniper configuration for the DHCP pool:\\n##\\nset system services dhcp pool BAS-POOL network 192.168.0.0/24\\nset system services dhcp pool BAS-POOL default-router 192.168.0.1\\nset system services dhcp pool BAS-POOL name-server 8.8.8.8\\nset system services dhcp pool BAS-POOL name-server 8.8.4.4\\nset system services dhcp pool BAS-POOL lease-time infinite\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, there isn\\'t a direct single command equivalent to Cisco\\'s \"ip dhcp pool\" that includes all parameters. The configuration is broken down into individual statements for each parameter under the DHCP pool.', 'trans_template': 'set system services dhcp pool BAS-POOL default-router 192.168.0.1'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set system services dhcp pool BAS-POOL name-server 8.8.8.8', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set system services dhcp pool BAS-POOL name-server 8.8.8.8', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent Juniper configuration for the DHCP pool:\\n##\\nset system services dhcp pool BAS-POOL network 192.168.0.0/24\\nset system services dhcp pool BAS-POOL default-router 192.168.0.1\\nset system services dhcp pool BAS-POOL name-server 8.8.8.8\\nset system services dhcp pool BAS-POOL name-server 8.8.4.4\\nset system services dhcp pool BAS-POOL lease-time infinite\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, there isn\\'t a direct single command equivalent to Cisco\\'s \"ip dhcp pool\" that includes all parameters. The configuration is broken down into individual statements for each parameter under the DHCP pool.', 'trans_template': 'set system services dhcp pool BAS-POOL name-server 8.8.8.8'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set system services dhcp pool BAS-POOL name-server 8.8.4.4', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set system services dhcp pool BAS-POOL name-server 8.8.4.4', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent Juniper configuration for the DHCP pool:\\n##\\nset system services dhcp pool BAS-POOL network 192.168.0.0/24\\nset system services dhcp pool BAS-POOL default-router 192.168.0.1\\nset system services dhcp pool BAS-POOL name-server 8.8.8.8\\nset system services dhcp pool BAS-POOL name-server 8.8.4.4\\nset system services dhcp pool BAS-POOL lease-time infinite\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, there isn\\'t a direct single command equivalent to Cisco\\'s \"ip dhcp pool\" that includes all parameters. The configuration is broken down into individual statements for each parameter under the DHCP pool.', 'trans_template': 'set system services dhcp pool BAS-POOL name-server 8.8.4.4'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set system services dhcp pool BAS-POOL lease-time infinite', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set system services dhcp pool BAS-POOL lease-time infinite', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent Juniper configuration for the DHCP pool:\\n##\\nset system services dhcp pool BAS-POOL network 192.168.0.0/24\\nset system services dhcp pool BAS-POOL default-router 192.168.0.1\\nset system services dhcp pool BAS-POOL name-server 8.8.8.8\\nset system services dhcp pool BAS-POOL name-server 8.8.4.4\\nset system services dhcp pool BAS-POOL lease-time infinite\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, there isn\\'t a direct single command equivalent to Cisco\\'s \"ip dhcp pool\" that includes all parameters. The configuration is broken down into individual statements for each parameter under the DHCP pool.', 'trans_template': 'set system services dhcp pool BAS-POOL lease-time infinite'}]]": 1,
    "['network [parameter1] [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set system services dhcp-local-server group BAS-POOL address-range low 192.168.0.1 high 192.168.0.254', 'parent_command': ['set system services dhcp pool BAS-POOL network 192.168.0.0/24'], 'root': 'set system services dhcp pool BAS-POOL network 192.168.0.0/24', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco DHCP pool network configuration:\\n\\n##\\nset system services dhcp-local-server group BAS-POOL address-range low 192.168.0.1 high 192.168.0.254\\n##\\n\\nNote: Juniper handles DHCP configuration differently than Cisco. Instead of specifying the network and mask directly, Juniper requires defining the actual address range to be assigned. The above command sets the assignable range for the BAS-POOL group to all usable addresses in the 192.168.0.0/24 subnet (excluding the network and broadcast addresses).\", 'trans_template': 'set system services dhcp-local-server group BAS-POOL address-range low 192.168.0.1 high 192.168.0.254'}]]": 1,
    "['default-router [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set access address-assignment pool BAS-POOL family inet default-router 192.168.0.1', 'parent_command': ['set system services dhcp pool BAS-POOL network 192.168.0.0/24'], 'root': 'set system services dhcp pool BAS-POOL network 192.168.0.0/24', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco `default-router` DHCP configuration command:\\n\\n##\\nset access address-assignment pool BAS-POOL family inet default-router 192.168.0.1\\n##\\n\\nAlternatively, if using DHCP local server configuration style in Junos:\\n\\n##\\nset system services dhcp pool BAS-POOL default-router 192.168.0.1\\n##\\n\\nNote: The exact syntax depends on whether you\\'re using Juniper\\'s \"access address-assignment\" (more modern) or \"system services dhcp\" (legacy) style configuration. Both are valid approaches.', 'trans_template': 'set access address-assignment pool BAS-POOL family inet default-router 192.168.0.1'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set system services dhcp pool BAS-POOL default-router 192.168.0.1', 'parent_command': ['set system services dhcp pool BAS-POOL network 192.168.0.0/24'], 'root': 'set system services dhcp pool BAS-POOL network 192.168.0.0/24', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco `default-router` DHCP configuration command:\\n\\n##\\nset access address-assignment pool BAS-POOL family inet default-router 192.168.0.1\\n##\\n\\nAlternatively, if using DHCP local server configuration style in Junos:\\n\\n##\\nset system services dhcp pool BAS-POOL default-router 192.168.0.1\\n##\\n\\nNote: The exact syntax depends on whether you\\'re using Juniper\\'s \"access address-assignment\" (more modern) or \"system services dhcp\" (legacy) style configuration. Both are valid approaches.', 'trans_template': 'set system services dhcp pool BAS-POOL default-router 192.168.0.1'}]]": 1,
